Backlog observations (not FAIL grounds — spec-inherited tradeoffs, not implementation defects):
1. Six live true pending→posted duplicates are still missed (Grammarly, BJ's Wholesale, BJ's
   Membership, Grubhub*FiveGuys x2, 4-day Amazon Mktplace) due to the spec's chosen 3-day window
   and 12-byte Description-prefix rule. If precision/recall gets revisited, OriginalDescription
   (not just Description) or a token-overlap match instead of a byte-prefix would catch the
   aggregator-name-vs-merchant-name and apostrophe/rewording cases.
2. The greedy pairing loop lets a closer-in-date shape-3 candidate steal a partner from a
   shape-1/2 candidate, potentially orphaning an existing decision on some future dataset even
   though it did not happen on the current live data. Pre-existing architecture, unchanged by
   design per spec's explicit scope fence.
